  "article": [
    {
      "level": 2,
      "heading": "Discussion",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Call this endpoint to get a customer’s refund history for your app. The response (`RefundLookupResponse`) includes up to 50 of the customer’s most-recently refunded transactions, based on the `revocationDate`.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.appstoreserverapi/documentation/AppStoreServerAPI/RefundLookupResponse",
            "doc://com.apple.appstoreserverapi/documentation/AppStoreServerAPI/revocationDate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "> **Note**\n>\n>  To get the complete refund history, use `Get-Refund-History`.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.appstoreserverapi/documentation/AppStoreServerAPI/Get-Refund-History"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "To call this endpoint, provide any original transaction identifier (`originalID`) for any of the customer’s in-app purchases. The response only includes App Store-approved refunds for any product type: consumable, non-consumable, auto-renewable subscriptions, and non-renewing subscriptions. For more information about product types, see `https://developer.apple.com/in-app-purchase/`.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/StoreKit/Transaction/originalID",
            "https://developer.apple.com/in-app-purchase/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The information in the response is the same as the information in one or more `REFUND` notifications (`notificationType`) from `AppStoreServerNotifications`. Use this API to retrieve any refund notifications you may have missed, such as during a server outage.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppStoreServerNotifications/notificationType",
            "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppStoreServerNotifications"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A successful response may have an empty `signedTransactions` array if the customer hasn’t received any App Store-approved refunds. To identify the date and reason code for a refund, see `revocationDate` and `revocationReason` in the `JWSTransactionDecodedPayload`.",
          "refs": [
            "doc://com.apple.appstoreserverapi/documentation/AppStoreServerAPI/JWSTransactionDecodedPayload"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The App Store Server API returns information based on the customer’s in-app purchase history regardless of whether the customer installs, removes, or reinstalls the app on their devices.",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    }
  ],
